Z||000014||LarryB||11-06-2001||06:23 PM||||Shaun, since you want to discuss responsibility, you might want to spend a few minutes and read RFC 1855.  One of the core guidelines is to either a) not post material others might find blatently objectionable or b) post it in a format that makes it clear to others they may find it objectionable.  A perfect example is the use on usenet of rot13 scrambler; if one sees a posting in that format they know it's potentially of questionable taste.  Another example is the [OT] qualifier in the headers of off-topic messages on mailing lists.<P><BR>Keep in mind as well that the majority of employers allow their employees to surf the 'net for their own personal enjoyment during lunch, breaks, etc....although material of questionable content is generally frowned upon. <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Shaun41178:<BR><B>Oh come on now.  Take some responsibility here people.  It says cars gone wild.  If you know anything about Girls Gone wild, and all you guys do, then you should know that it might have somethign liek that in it.  Besides hot cars and hot women always go togethor.<P>And come on cooter.  You were the 8th person to post to this thread.  Didn't you read any of the previous posts?  I mean how many other people said the words boobs or something in their post about the video.  <P>And why are you downloading PFF at school anyways?  Thats time for school not looking at cars.  And Larry come on man you are at work.  Do some work, not look at PFF.  Wait till you get home to look at PFF.  And before you download another file maybe you should take a look at some of the posts to see if there is any chance that there is something on the link that you don't think someone else would appreciate seeing.  Take some responsibility for yourselves</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
